==By state==
The PVIs for states are calculated based on the results of the U.S. presidential elections in [[2016 United States presidential election|2020]] and [[2024 United States presidential election|2024]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-03-06 |title=2025 Cook PVI℠: State Map and List |url=https://www.cookpolitical.com/cook-pvi/2025-partisan-voting-index/state-map-and-list |url-access=subscription|access-date=2025-05-10 |website=Cook Political Report |language=en}}</ref> The table below reflects the state of Congress and governors, based on the 2024 election results.

Using the [[United States Census Bureau]]'s official [[Demographics of the United States#Population table|2024 population estimates]], a combined 182,737,780 residents live in the 29 states that lean [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]]; 141,264,067 residents live in the 20 voting blocs (19 states plus [[Washington, D.C.]]) that lean [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]]; and 16,101,434 residents live in the two states ([[Michigan]] and [[Wisconsin]]) that lean neither Republican nor Democratic (PVI of EVEN).

